# Interactive-ready controls

**Activation:** when adding or changing SPA views, loading states, overlays, or thin-hook fetch shapes.

## Law

> If a control is not ready, do not show it. If it is shown, it must be immediately interactive.

## Definitions

- **Control** — link, button, combobox, tab, sort header, pagination link, or form field with submit.
- **Ready** — backing data/state exists for the control's action; no in-flight fetch blocks the action.
- **Shown** — visible in the layout (not `hidden`, not zero-size, not inside a collapsed panel the user has not opened).

## Required patterns

1. **First paint, zero data** — full-page `LoadingMessage` / skeleton with **no** interactive chrome (Search, TypeDetail pattern).
2. **Refetch with prior data** — `keepPreviousData` + `tableBusy` / `sectionBusy`: dim + `aria-busy`, **never** `pointer-events-none` on containers holding links ([`JobList.tsx`](hpcperfstats/site/frontend/src/views/JobList.tsx) test contract).
3. **Secondary sections** — hide, collapse, or skeleton until ready; fetch on expand/tab (JobList filter options + distributions).
4. **User-initiated in-flight action** — `disabled` on the **same** button the user clicked (`rotating` on PageApiKey) is allowed.
5. **Bokeh** — defer embed until section visible (`deferEmbedUntilVisible` default); no Unavailable while `isLoading` ([`design-focused-spa-ux.mdc`](design-focused-spa-ux.mdc), [`job-plot-artifacts-caching.mdc`](job-plot-artifacts-caching.mdc)).

## Forbidden patterns

- `pointer-events-none` on a parent wrapping sort links, table rows, or pagination (except `aria-hidden` decorative spans).
- In-page sticky headers/tabs above **`--z-sticky-inpage`** (10) except portaled modal/floating UI — never reuse modal-tier z-index (e.g. `z-1010`) on table headers.
- Visible combobox/select/button rendered `disabled` while options or section data load — use skeleton rows or omit the control ([`JobListHeaderFilters.tsx`](hpcperfstats/site/frontend/src/components/JobListHeaderFilters.tsx)).
- Full-page skeleton replacing an already-rendered interactive surface on refetch.
- Mounting Bokeh into `hidden` or zero-size subtrees.
- Modal backdrop blocking unrelated page chrome when `modal={false}` — omit overlay ([`dialog.tsx`](hpcperfstats/site/frontend/src/components/ui/dialog.tsx) `showOverlay={false}`).
- Focus trap stealing Tab when focus is outside the trapped panel ([`useFocusTrap.ts`](hpcperfstats/site/frontend/src/hooks/useFocusTrap.ts)).

## Thin-hook loading shapes

| Flag | Meaning |
|------|---------|
| `initialLoading` | `isLoading && !data` — first payload only; may gate full-page skeleton |
| `tableBusy` / `detailBusy` / `sectionBusy` | `isFetching && !isLoading` with stale data visible — dim only, keep interactive |
| `optionsLoading` / `sectionInitialLoading` | Scoped to one panel; must not gate entire page |

Reference hooks: [`use-job-list.ts`](hpcperfstats/site/frontend/src/hooks/use-job-list.ts), [`use-job-detail.ts`](hpcperfstats/site/frontend/src/hooks/use-job-detail.ts), [`use-admin-monitor-section.ts`](hpcperfstats/site/frontend/src/hooks/use-admin-monitor-section.ts).

## Reference implementations

- **JobList** — table first; deferred `filter_options`; lazy histograms; `JobList.test.tsx` (`tableBusy` not pointer-blocked).
- **JobDetail** — `initialLoading` only on first paint; tabs stay mounted during `detailsLoading`; deep-link test in `JobDetail.test.tsx`.

## Tests

- Extend Vitest when changing loading UX: assert shown controls lack blocking `pointer-events-none` on parent containers.
- Run drift guard: `src/utils/interactive-ready-drift.test.ts`.

